obvious you want to write stories about&nbsp;
ancient mythology, folklore, fairy tales,

00:14:44.640 --> 00:14:49.020
stuff like Thor or the Baba Yaga or The Little&nbsp;
Mermaid, you are almost certainly in the clear

00:14:49.020 --> 00:14:52.620
as long as what you write isn't taken from&nbsp;
other modern interpretations of those same

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:56.340
ideas. Other things that you should be good to&nbsp;
use are urban legends and cryptids, stuff like:

00:14:56.340 --> 00:15:00.060
Bigfoot, Mothman, Bloody Mary.
No single person owns those ideas,

00:15:00.060 --> 00:15:03.240
and you could just make some incredibly&nbsp;
unique stories using them as jumping off

00:15:03.240 --> 00:15:07.140
points. This also applies if you want to create&nbsp;
something using basic ideas to build off of,

00:15:07.140 --> 00:15:11.640
like with The Backrooms. Take the same idea that&nbsp;
Kane used as the basis for a series and then build

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:17.400
your own ideas on top of it, away from Kane’s.
You don't need to use Async or project KV31 or

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:21.420
the Lifeform Fellow to tell a compelling story&nbsp;
about The Backrooms. All you gotta do is take

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:25.920
an idea that you like and change it enough that&nbsp;
it becomes your own thing. Great example of this:

00:15:25.920 --> 00:15:31.440
The Enderman from Minecraft. They were originally&nbsp;
spoofs of Slenderman. I mean, the name alone makes

00:15:31.440 --> 00:15:35.400
it pretty darn obvious. But over the years, the&nbsp;
Enderman have had their own quirks and lore added,

00:15:35.400 --> 00:15:39.720
they've become completely unique from their&nbsp;
slender origins. You can do the exact same thing;

00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:43.560
using ideas that you like and then changing&nbsp;
them enough to make them yours and yours alone.

00:15:43.560 --> 00:15:47.820
So all of that protects you and your work.
But what if we want to protect the collective

00:15:47.820 --> 00:15:52.020
works? Stuff like the incredible community driven&nbsp;
lore that's popped up around The Backrooms? Well,

00:15:52.020 --> 00:15:56.520
we have the perfect template to look to with&nbsp;
the SCP wiki. If you somehow don't know, the SCP

00:15:56.520 --> 00:16:00.660
Foundation is a collaborative writing project&nbsp;
where users submit articles about fictional

00:16:00.660 --> 00:16:05.760
objects, locations and characters, all inspired&nbsp;
by elements of horror, sci-fi and urban fantasy.

00:16:05.760 --> 00:16:10.080
A lot of this content is similar in tone to The&nbsp;
Backrooms. Once an article is approved to go up

00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:14.400
on the website, though, anyone is free to take the&nbsp;
ideas from that article and add it to their own

00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:20.040
work, both on and off the SCP website. Everything&nbsp;
published on the SCP wiki is done through the

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:25.440
Creative Commons attribution-sharealike&nbsp;
3.0 license or CC-BY-SA for short.

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:30.660
That means that anyone is free to make content&nbsp;
based on SCPs. They can even make money. But

00:16:30.660 --> 00:16:35.400
they have to credit the original authors and&nbsp;
then also publish their work under that same

00:16:35.400 --> 00:16:39.420
sharealike license. That means that yes,&nbsp;
anyone from an indie game dev to a major

00:16:39.420 --> 00:16:44.340
movie studio can profit from the SCP wiki and&nbsp;
their articles, but the ideas that they add

00:16:44.340 --> 00:16:49.140
to the SCP must also be free for anyone&nbsp;
else to use, publish and profit from.

00:16:49.140 --> 00:16:52.920
Though this might not work for everything,&nbsp;
this is an awesome system for these sorts of

00:16:52.920 --> 00:16:56.460
collaborative projects. And maybe the single&nbsp;
most important thing to keep in mind about

00:16:56.460 --> 00:17:00.960
all of this: support the independent writers&nbsp;
and artists that you love so they can keep

00:17:00.960 --> 00:17:05.280
creating. Read the work of these creators, share&nbsp;
them with your friends, help spread the word.

00:17:05.280 --> 00:17:08.820
One of my particular favorites that I haven't&nbsp;
seen reach the same level of success is The

00:17:08.820 --> 00:17:14.040
Backrooms or SCP yet are the short stories by&nbsp;
the Reddit user SearchAndRescueWoods. They have

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:17.820
a series about these mysterious staircases&nbsp;
just appearing out in the woods and their

00:17:17.820 --> 00:17:22.800
connections to missing persons. It is great.
Remember, the next Backrooms, Slenderman and

00:17:22.800 --> 00:17:27.120
SCP Foundation is out there somewhere just&nbsp;
waiting to be discovered. So please share

00:17:27.120 --> 00:17:30.000
some of your favorites down in the comments.&nbsp;
And check out what everyone else is posting

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:33.000
down there. I know I'll be excited to see&nbsp;
what you guys are saying down there because

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:37.320
who knows? Maybe one day it'll appear here&nbsp;
in a theory. Until that day comes though,

